Oh okay, so the server has direct access to the files. That's much better than what I'd thought, that the files lived on the user's system.

In that case, it'll have to be custom inputs and server side scripting, like your example with the text box. There's no built-in way to do this.

If you don't want to use a 3rd party library, you could make it easier on users by having them select from a list of files instead.
Use list.files() to list the files on the drive, and put some sort of UI around it. That's pretty much what shinyFiles does as well.

