Yeah, that's a totally valid strategy--I've used something similar myself at times. The only thing I would tell you is to absolutely NOT source(fname) UNLESS you have whitelisted the value of fname to be one that you're aware is legitimate (and I do not mean file.exists, but rather, hardcode the filenames that are legitimate). This is to prevent a malicious user from being able to execute literally any .R file they can get onto the server.

