I'd try ssh-ing into the server with sudo access, then do "sudo su - shiny" to switch to the "shiny" user, then launch R and see if you can successfully library(plotly). If that doesn't work then you'll know you didn't successfully install plotly as a system library. You can either install it in the shiny user's personal library, or try again with the system library, or try packrat <https://rstudio.github.io/packrat/>.

